  <prompt>Owner UAT round 4 (A1, 2026-11-15): the Create Project wizard's Description has no AI draft, while Create Matter's Enter Info does. Owner 2026-11-28: fix every open 185 item.</prompt>
  <role>Implementer agent, worktree off origin/master, PR to master.</role>
  <goal>Create Project's Enter Info shows a "Generate with AI" button beside Project Description that behaves like Create Matter's (enabled once the name is entered, streams a draft into the description, the user can edit it), in every host (Console in-app wizard and the code page).</goal>
  <context><background>
Reference implementation: src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateMatterWizard/CreateRecordStep.tsx:498 (handleGenerateSummary) and :629-645 (button); service CreateMatterWizard/matterService.ts:579 streamAiDraftSummary, POST {bff}/api/workspace/matters/ai-summary (SSE). BFF: src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Workspace/WorkspaceMatterEndpoints.cs:63-65 maps the route, handler HandleAiSummary (:158); ConsumerTypes.cs:58 registers consumer id ai-summary. Target: CreateProjectWizard/CreateProjectStep.tsx:484-501 (a plain Textarea plus AiFieldTag).
  </background></context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md 11">Default to reuse: extend the existing endpoint, handler and service (for example an optional record kind plus the project's own descriptive fields) rather than add a new endpoint, unless the handler cannot be extended without changing matter behaviour; state the three justification answers in the PR either way.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md 10">BFF hygiene: placement, the AI PublicContracts facade (ADR-013), publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new HIGH CVE, tests. Matter requests must produce the same prompt as today.</constraint>
    <constraint source="reuse">Share the client streaming helper between matter and project instead of copying it; the button may become a small shared piece if both steps use it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="process">Do not edit current-task.md, TASK-INDEX.md, POMLs or defer-issues.md. No git stash. No sub-agents. Run dotnet test tests/Spaarke.ArchTests and a filtered Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests run (Workspace), never the unfiltered suite. Run the client-lint ratchet before pushing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public repo">No environment ids in code, tests, commits or PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>
  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read HandleAiSummary and the prompt it builds; decide the extension shape; keep the matter path unchanged (test it).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the project path (project name and the type/area fields the project has) with tests.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the button and handler to CreateProjectStep, reusing the matter helper; jest tests (disabled without a name, streams into the field, an error shows the existing AI error treatment).</step>
    <step order="4">PR body: the section 11 answers, publish-size delta, ADR-013 note. The dev BFF deploy goes through uac-r2; the main session asks.</step>
  </steps>
  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF tests: the matter request is unchanged (must-not-fire), a project request builds a project prompt (must-fire), bad input is refused; ArchTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Jest: CreateProjectStep button tests pass; CreateMatter tests unchanged and passing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no second streaming helper; no new endpoint unless the PR states why extension was impossible.</criterion>
